            <ArticleTitle>The principles of cancer staging.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>ed61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3332/ecancer.2016.ed61</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The anatomic disease extent or tumour stage of a cancer at diagnosis as a determinant of prognosis is discussed. The importance of cancer stage in individual patient prognosis and determination of treatment is reviewed as well as its value in research and cancer control activities. The conflict between the need for stability of cancer stage definitions over time and the need to evolve with advances in medicine are examined. The ecancer elearning modules on Cancer Stage are introduced.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
